# 🚀 Laravel Backend Coding Standards

## ✅ Architecture

- [ ] Follow MVC strictly (Controller → Service → Model)
- [ ] Controllers must be thin (no business logic)
- [ ] Business logic should be in Service classes
- [ ] Use Repository pattern where needed
- [ ] Reuse logic via Services/Traits (avoid duplication)

---

## ✅ Database & Eloquent

- [ ] Avoid N+1 queries (use eager loading with `with()`)
- [ ] Never write DB queries in Controllers
- [ ] Use Eloquent ORM instead of raw queries (unless necessary)
- [ ] Select only required columns (no `*`)
- [ ] Use `chunk()` or `cursor()` for large datasets
- [ ] Use bulk insert/update instead of loops

---

## ✅ Query Optimization

- [ ] Use proper indexing on frequently queried columns
- [ ] Avoid functions on indexed columns in WHERE
- [ ] Use `whereIn` instead of multiple OR conditions
- [ ] Avoid unnecessary joins
- [ ] Cache heavy queries using Redis

---

## ✅ Error Handling & Logging

- [ ] Use try-catch for critical operations
- [ ] Log exceptions using `Log::error()`
- [ ] Never expose raw errors to users
- [ ] Add API request/response logs where needed

---

## ✅ Validation & Security

- [ ] Use Form Request classes for validation
- [ ] Never trust user input (sanitize everything)
- [ ] Use `.env` for sensitive configs
- [ ] Prevent SQL injection (no unsafe raw queries)

---

## ✅ Code Quality

- [ ] Use proper naming conventions (camelCase for methods)
- [ ] Keep functions small and single-purpose
- [ ] Avoid deep nesting (>3 levels)
- [ ] Add meaningful comments where required

---

## ✅ Queues & Jobs

- [ ] Use Jobs for heavy operations
- [ ] Ensure jobs are retry-safe
- [ ] Log job failures
- [ ] Avoid long-running synchronous tasks

---

## ✅ API Standards

- [ ] Use Resource classes for API responses
- [ ] Return proper HTTP status codes
- [ ] Maintain consistent response structure

---

## 🚫 Avoid

- [ ] DB queries in Controllers
- [ ] N+1 queries
- [ ] `dd()`, `dump()` in production
- [ ] Hardcoded values